# Plan — the blog-forge brief for the Image Processing pillar

## Context

You want one **L4 pillar post on image processing** that acts as the parent of a
series. The pain it addresses: image processing is the topic where the math loses
people — too many algorithms, no shared frame, and explainers that either hand-wave
the math or dump it without showing how anyone actually evaluates it.

So this post's job is the **foundations and the map**: what image processing *is*,
everything it considers, taught through the math and the signal view, with advanced
OpenCV as the tooling lens. It deliberately does **not** cover every corner — each
area names the child post that will go deep on it later.

Constraints you set: strictly math + signals + OpenCV; explain it in a very simple
way alongside the math, because readers otherwise cannot follow how the math is
evaluated, how a signal is detected, or how the notebook experiment works; and **do
not install or persist anything** — math only, with the libraries and functions shown
as examples at the end.

The deliverable of this plan is **only the brief handed to blog-forge**. Pipeline
mechanics, figure rendering and file locations are already handled and are not
restated here.

